# Load-bearing identifiers the privacy check may find in prose, one Python regex per line. Prose names roles, not
# repositories, people, logins or hostnames (docs/adr/0013-prose-names-roles-not-names.md); a match the check
# reports passes only when it lies wholly inside a match of one of these. tools/validate/homelab-validate and CI
# (.github/workflows/validate.yaml) pass each as --privacy-allow through validate_args.py.
#
# Keep each one narrow: a path, a key prefix, a file name or a pinned install URL. Never a bare hostname, login
# or name. The denylist itself is never committed (the PRIVACY_DENYLIST secret).
#
# The stack root as a path.
(?<![\w@.-])nc8kg1101/
# .env keys, keyed by Host.
HOPS_NC8KG1101_
# The Host's doco-cd deploy config, and its bootstrap wizard (since removed) as the ops Stack's comments cite it.
\.doco-cd\.nc8kg1101\.yml
scripts/bootstrap-nc8kg1101\.sh
# An ADR's file name, in links to it.
0007-custom-components-from-homelab-components\.md
# Pinned installs of the shared Repo Tooling and its release assets.
git\+https://github\.com/jbruns/homelab-components@[\w.-]+#subdirectory=[\w/-]+
https://github\.com/jbruns/homelab-components/releases/download/\$STARTUP_ORDER_TAG/startup-order\.sh
